[{:db/id 17592186119824 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-22cb5720-988d-5f1f-bf8b-00932134f7ba"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186351160 :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=-{b}_{2}$, ${c}_{2}=2{b}_{3}$ and ${c}_{3}={b}_{1}?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119825 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-462a3ac8-3692-5123-988e-2869c674b5a5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186351164 :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=4{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}=2{b}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "We are given that\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}=4{b}_{1}+{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}=2{b}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the $b$'s in terms of $c$'s. From the second equation, we get \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=4(\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2})+{b}_{2}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{2}={c}_{1}-2{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSince $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]$, we can write the vector $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={b}_{1}-7{b}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2}-7({c}_{1}-2{c}_{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2}-7{c}_{1}+14{c}_{2} \\\\  & =-7{c}_{1}+\\frac{29}{2}{c}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ \\frac{29}{2}\\end{aligned}].$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-22cb5720-988d-5f1f-bf8b-00932134f7ba" :question/id #uuid "22cb5720-988d-5f1f-bf8b-00932134f7ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-112811" :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=-3{b}_{2}$, ${c}_{2}=2{b}_{3}$ and ${c}_{3}=3{b}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =3{b}_{1}+6{b}_{2}-2{b}_{3} \\\\  & =6{b}_{2}-2{b}_{3}+3{b}_{1} \\\\  & =-2(-3{b}_{2})-2{b}_{3}+3{b}_{1} \\\\  & =-2{c}_{1}-{c}_{2}+{c}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f107fe79-1c11-5ad7-9f21-fcda8e8329e0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f107fe79-1c11-5ad7-9f21-fcda8e8329e0" :answer-field/id #uuid "f107fe79-1c11-5ad7-9f21-fcda8e8329e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8e9f3805-6ec3-52b0-8981-651c4924ab5e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8e9f3805-6ec3-52b0-8981-651c4924ab5e" "answer-75100d18-03f7-5132-bc07-08e656b29767" "answer-48c04403-8948-5cde-b72e-bcbd3cd68850" "answer-90fa75ef-f7b2-5f35-896b-4536657baef3" "answer-1ec99580-87ff-5cfa-9a50-83210750a588"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e9f3805-6ec3-52b0-8981-651c4924ab5e" :answer/id #uuid "8e9f3805-6ec3-52b0-8981-651c4924ab5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-75100d18-03f7-5132-bc07-08e656b29767" :answer/id #uuid "75100d18-03f7-5132-bc07-08e656b29767" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48c04403-8948-5cde-b72e-bcbd3cd68850" :answer/id #uuid "48c04403-8948-5cde-b72e-bcbd3cd68850" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-90fa75ef-f7b2-5f35-896b-4536657baef3" :answer/id #uuid "90fa75ef-f7b2-5f35-896b-4536657baef3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1ec99580-87ff-5cfa-9a50-83210750a588" :answer/id #uuid "1ec99580-87ff-5cfa-9a50-83210750a588" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186380636 :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=4{b}_{3}$, ${c}_{2}=2{b}_{1}$ and ${c}_{3}=3{b}_{2}?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-462a3ac8-3692-5123-988e-2869c674b5a5" :question/id #uuid "462a3ac8-3692-5123-988e-2869c674b5a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-113098" :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=-2{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}=-2{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We are given that\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}=-2{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}=-2{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the $b$'s in terms of $c$'s. From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n{b}_{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{c}_{2}=-2{b}_{1}+(-\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1})\\,⟹\\,{b}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{4}{c}_{1}-\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSince $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$, we can write the vector $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-8{b}_{1}+6{b}_{2} \\\\  & =-8(-\\frac{1}{4}{c}_{1}-\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2})+6(-\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}) \\\\  & =2{c}_{1}+4{c}_{2}-3{c}_{1} \\\\  & =-{c}_{1}+4{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f715ad10-8843-5e87-a878-4728db817271"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f715ad10-8843-5e87-a878-4728db817271" :answer-field/id #uuid "f715ad10-8843-5e87-a878-4728db817271" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-22b18ee1-002f-5c66-b260-413039c7fa38" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d19d735a-e23a-5d22-b726-fc09edb321eb" "answer-22b18ee1-002f-5c66-b260-413039c7fa38" "answer-11a1b0ee-a4a2-5576-8c66-7aaec2ee0e69" "answer-44ad6232-afa5-5eee-acd4-ac7923c6c4c4" "answer-54f9c040-8ec5-5672-a995-f18c78ec39cf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d19d735a-e23a-5d22-b726-fc09edb321eb" :answer/id #uuid "d19d735a-e23a-5d22-b726-fc09edb321eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-22b18ee1-002f-5c66-b260-413039c7fa38" :answer/id #uuid "22b18ee1-002f-5c66-b260-413039c7fa38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-11a1b0ee-a4a2-5576-8c66-7aaec2ee0e69" :answer/id #uuid "11a1b0ee-a4a2-5576-8c66-7aaec2ee0e69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-44ad6232-afa5-5eee-acd4-ac7923c6c4c4" :answer/id #uuid "44ad6232-afa5-5eee-acd4-ac7923c6c4c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-54f9c040-8ec5-5672-a995-f18c78ec39cf" :answer/id #uuid "54f9c040-8ec5-5672-a995-f18c78ec39cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [: